{{also|Verso|versó|versò}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|[[in]] [[versō]] [[foliō]]||on the turned leaf, on the turned page}}, the [[Appendix:Glossary#ablative case|ablative case]] of the Latin {{m|la|versus||turned, changed}} from the perfect passive participle of {{m|la|vertō||turn}}. Compare {{m|la|rēctus||right}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɜː(ɹ)səʊ|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The back side of a flat object which is to be examined visually, as for reading, such as a sheet or a leaf or a [[coin]] or a [[medal]].
# {{lb|en|printing}} The [[left-hand]] [[page]] of a [[book]] of a script which reads from left to right, usually having an even page number.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|back side of a flat object}} {{l|en|back}}, {{l|en|flipside}}, {{l|en|backside}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|back side of a flat object}} {{l|en|recto}}, {{l|en|obverse}}

